# Public repository: only the core code and its configuration are tracked.
#
# Everything else stays on the author's machine only: assistant notes, prompts
# and logs, planning documents, the report sources and PDFs, run outputs, virtual
# environments, caches and archives.
#
# This file is an allow-list. Every top-level entry is ignored, then the entries
# below are re-included. New files under src/, scripts/ and tests/ are picked up
# automatically; anything else at the top level must be listed here to be tracked.
/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/pyproject.toml
!/uv.lock
!/requirements.txt
!/src/
!/scripts/
!/tests/

# Never track debris, even inside the allowed directories.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
*.icloud
.env
.env.*
